millerX is a small native GTK 3 file browser with Miller columns: every
folder from / down to the current one sits in its own column, and the
selected file is previewed on the right (pictures, the first page of
PDFs, text, the contents of zip/tar archives, folder sizes). Folders
show their pictures and PDFs as a fast thumbnail gallery, using the
shared ~/.cache/thumbnails like Thunar does.

Copy/paste, drag and drop, bookmarks shared with Thunar and the GTK
file dialogs, USB drives (udisks2), per-folder sorting, properties with
editable permissions, packing and unpacking archives (libarchive), and
"Open as root" through polkit (pkexec).

Everything it needs is part of Slackware. Programs it uses if they are
installed (all in Slackware too):

  poppler (pdftoppm)  first page of PDFs
  ffmpeg              AVIF, HEIC and other pictures that gdk-pixbuf
                      can't read, video frames, music covers
  polkit agent        "Open as root"

Building needs a fully patched Slackware 15.0 (meson 0.60 or newer).
